    "description": "FlapJacked leans harder on protein than Kodiak. Retailer labels at the time of writing list about 20 g of protein per half-cup (roughly 53 g) serving for about 200 calories, with around 5 g of fiber, using whey protein as the main protein source. That is the highest protein-to-calorie ratio of the boxed mixes here. The trade-off is texture: with more whey and less flour, buyers report denser cakes that dry out if overcooked. A separately labeled gluten-free version exists, so check which pouch a listing is selling.",
    "pros": [
      "About 20 g of protein per half-cup serving per retailer labels",
      "Roughly 200 calories per serving, the best protein-to-calorie ratio here",
      "Doubles as a baking mix for muffins and mug cakes"
    ],
    "cons": [
      "Denser and drier than Kodiak if you overcook it, per buyer reports",
      "Ingredient lists differ by retailer (whey isolate vs concentrate), so read the pouch",
      "Smaller pouch sizes mean a higher cost per serving than grocery boxes"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "The pick when protein per serving matters more than a classic diner texture.",
    "specs": {
      "Protein / serving": "About 20 g per half cup (label)",
      "Calories": "About 200",
      "Protein source": "Whey protein plus flour blend",
      "Best for": "Highest protein from a box"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "birch-benders-protein-pancake-waffle-mix",
    "name": "Birch Benders Protein Pancake & Waffle Mix",
    "brand": "Birch Benders",
    "badge": "Best Just-Add-Water",
    "category": "Complete protein pancake and waffle mix",
    "description": "Birch Benders sells its protein mix as a complete, just-add-water batter, which makes it the least-effort option here. Retailer labels at the time of writing list about 15 to 16 g of protein per serving, depending on whether the box uses a half-cup or third-cup serving, with roughly eight or nine servings in a 16 oz box. Buyers describe a lighter, slightly sweeter pancake than Kodiak. Birch Benders also makes a separate plant protein mix with less protein per serving, so check the box name.",
    "pros": [
      "About 15 to 16 g of protein per serving with water only, per retailer labels",
